; npm configuration used exclusively by the Azure DevOps build pipelines.
;
; This file deliberately lives outside the repository root so that it is NOT picked
; up by `npm install` for anyone who clones the repository. Open source contributors
; and the GitHub Actions workflows keep restoring from the public npm registry, while
; the internal ADO pipelines opt in via the `npm_config_userconfig` environment
; variable so that package restore is routed through the Central Feed Service (CFS).
;
; Required by SFI Network Isolation: build pipelines must not reach public package
; feeds directly. npm rewrites the host of every `resolved` URL in package-lock.json
; to the registry configured here, so the lockfile can keep its public npmjs URLs.

registry=https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/mseng/VSJava/_packaging/vscjava/npm/registry/
always-auth=true
